/*! @page disagg_role_management Managing disaggregated storage roles

In disaggregated storage, the application decides which node owns shared writes and coordinates
elections, replication, and the handoff between nodes. WiredTiger provides leader and follower
roles so the application can choose which node persists data to shared storage without
restarting the connections.

This page describes roles from the application's perspective, including configuration,
expected call sequences, and restrictions. See @ref arch-disagg-roles for their architecture
and implementation.

@section disagg_role_management_roles Leader and follower

There are two roles: the leader and the follower.

The <b>leader</b> accepts application writes and persists their changes in shared storage through
checkpoints. A <b>follower</b> accepts replicated writes and stores their changes locally,
without persisting them to shared storage. Both serve reads from shared data: a leader reads the
current data, while a follower reads the most recent checkpoint it adopted, together with newer
replicated changes it applied locally.

| Responsibility | Leader | Follower |
|----------------|--------|----------|
| Accepted writes | Application writes | Writes replicated from the leader |
| Where changes are persisted | Shared storage through checkpoints | Not persisted to shared storage by this node |
| Readable data | Current data | Shared checkpointed data and newer local changes |
| Shared checkpoints | Produces them | Adopts checkpoints produced by the leader |

Once an adopted checkpoint contains a change, the follower can remove its local copy when it is
no longer needed by readers. Frequent leader checkpoints and follower checkpoint adoption
therefore reduce the amount of data followers must retain locally. A local copy is not removed
merely because a checkpoint was produced; the follower must first adopt it, and removal must be
safe for existing readers.

Keeping changes locally does not persist them to shared storage. Applications remain
responsible for replication and for replaying changes needed after a restart.

@htmlonly
